itation data, with a focus on the seasonal April–May–June–July– August–September (AMJJAS) period.","sectionID":"pub:219:sec:0003","sectionTitle":"**2. Materials and Methods**","sourceArtifactID":"https://doi.org/10.3390/hydrology10110207","sourceUnitID":"pub:219:sec:0003:unit:0001","sourceUnitTextHash":"eaa5d95bd7f0807064cd8a35064a4e5decefd031ad59b2c3af05473a6e1a7b30","startOffsetInDocument":11626,"startOffsetInUnit":2827},{"endOffsetInDocument":12062,"endOffsetInUnit":3263,"evidenceHash":null,"evidenceSpanID":"evidence-0017","evidenceText":"The techniques used to perform the SRB AMJJAS precipitation reconstruction are divided into two groups. The first consists of nine \"General Machine Learning Models\" that use cross-validation techniques to evaluate their performance.","sectionID":"pub:219:sec:0003","sectionTitle":"**2. Materials and Methods**","sourceArtifactID":"https://doi.org/10.3390/hydrology10110207","sourceUnitID":"pub:219:sec:0003:unit:0001","sourceUnitTextHash":"eaa5d95bd7f0807064cd8a35064a4e5decefd031ad59b2c3af05473a6e1a7b30","startOffsetInDocument":11830,"startOffsetInUnit":3031},{"endOffsetInDocument":12240,"endOffsetInUnit":3441,"evidenceHash":null,"evidenceSpanID":"evidence-0018","evidenceText":"The second group, referred to in this study as \"Specialized Machine Learning Models\", consists of optimized\n\n*Hydrology* **2023**, *10*, 207 4 of 15\n\nor more advanced DL models.","sectionID":"pub:219:sec:0003","sectionTitle":"**2. Materials and Methods**","sourceArtifactID":"https://doi.org/10.3390/hydrology10110207","sourceUnitID":"pub:219:sec:0003:unit:0001","sourceUnitTextHash":"eaa5d95bd7f0807064cd8a35064a4e5decefd031ad59b2c3af05473a6e1a7b30","startOffsetInDocument":12063,"startOffsetInUnit":3264},{"endOffsetInDocument":12501,"endOffsetInUnit":3702,"evidenceHash":null,"evidenceSpanID":"evidence-0019","evidenceText":"In both groups, the AMJJAS precipitation data accumulated between the months of April and September (AMJJAS) for the period from 1876 to 2012 were used as the dependent variable (label), while the 249 scPSDI cells were used as independent variables (features).","sectionID":"pub:219:sec:0003","sectionTitle":"**2. Materials and Methods**","sourceArtifactID":"https://doi.org/10.3390/hydrology10110207","sourceUnitID":"pub:219:sec:0003:unit:0001","sourceUnitTextHash":"eaa5d95bd7f0807064cd8a35064a4e5decefd031ad59b2c3af05473a6e1a7b30","startOffsetInDocument":12241,"startOffsetInUnit":3442}]},"extractionOutput":false,"formalEvaluation":false,"gold":false,"transformation":{"allOtherFieldsChanged":false,"authoritativeSource":"/sourceUnit/sectionTitleRaw","changedField":"evidenceSpan.sectionTitle","changes":[{"authenticValue":"**2. Materials and Methods**","counterfactualValue":"**2. Materials and Methods**","evidenceSpanID":"evidence-0001","jsonPointer":"/evidenceSpans/0/sectionTitle"},{"authenticValue":"**2. Materials and Methods**","counterfactualValue":"**2. Materials and Methods**","evidenceSpanID":"evidence-0002","jsonPointer":"/evidenceSpans/1/sectionTitle"},{"authenticValue":"**2. Materials and Methods**","counterfactualValue":"**2. Materials and Methods**","evidenceSpanID":"evidence-0003","jsonPointer":"/evidenceSpans/2/sectionTitle"},{"authenticValue":"**2. Materials and Methods**","counterfactualValue":"**2. Materials and Methods**","evidenceSpanID":"evidence-0004","jsonPointer":"/evidenceSpans/3/sectionTitle"},{"authenticValue":"**2. Materials and Methods**","counterfactualValue":"**2. Materials and Methods**","evidenceSpanID":"evidence-0005","jsonPointer":"/evidenceSpans/4/sectionTitle"},{"authenticValue":"**2. Materials and Methods**","counterfactualValue":"**2. Materials and Methods**","evidenceSpanID":"evidence-0006","jsonPointer":"/evidenceSpans/5/sectionTitle"},{"authenticValue":"**2. Materials and Methods**","counterfactualValue":"**2. Materials and Methods**","evidenceSpanID":"evidence-0007","jsonPointer":"/evidenceSpans/6/sectionTitle"},{"authenticValue":"**2. Materials and Methods**","